module hi-circuit-court-civil.civil

import hi-state-rules.{ ActionCommenced, JudgmentEntered, NoticeOfAppealFiled }

start complaint-filed

state complaint-filed: "Complaint filed" by applicant cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 3"
{
  note "A civil action is commenced by filing a complaint with the court (Haw. R. Civ. P. 3); the complaint is accompanied by a civil information sheet filed with it (Haw. R. Civ. P. 3.1(a)). Upon filing the clerk issues a summons, which is served together with the complaint (Haw. R. Civ. P. 4(a), (d)). Periods in this package are stated, not counted: Rule 6(a) excludes the trigger day, includes the last day unless it is a Saturday, Sunday or holiday, and excludes intermediate Saturdays, Sundays and holidays from a period of less than 7 days; 'holiday' is a day so designated under HRS § 8-1; 2 days are added after service by mail (Haw. R. Civ. P. 6(a), (e)). The filing fee is not stated in the vendored rules. The earlier outline named no leading decision for this step."
  edge-complaint-filed-served "Summons and complaint served" -> answer-due {
    event ActionCommenced()
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 4"
  }
}

decision answer-due: "Answer, motion or default" by office cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 12(a)"
{
  note "A defendant serves an answer within 20 days after being served with the summons and complaint, except when service is made under Rule 4(c) and a different time is prescribed in an order of court under a statute or rule of court. A Rule 12 motion alters the period: if the court denies it or postpones its disposition to trial, the responsive pleading is served within 10 days after notice of the court's action; if it grants a more definite statement, within 10 days after service of that statement (Haw. R. Civ. P. 12(a)(1), (3))."
  edge-answer-due-default "No plea or defense" -> default-entered {
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 55(a)"
  }
  edge-answer-due-motion "Rule 12(b) motion" -> pleading-motion {
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 12(b)"
  }
  edge-answer-due-answer "Answer served" -> discovery { authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 12(a)" }
}

decision pleading-motion: "Motion to dismiss decided" by court cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 12(b)"
{
  note "The defenses of Rule 12(b)(1)-(7) may be made by motion, before pleading if a further pleading is permitted; if matters outside the pleading are presented on a 12(b)(6) motion and not excluded, it is treated as one for summary judgment under Rule 56 (Haw. R. Civ. P. 12(b)). A written motion and notice of its hearing are served not less than 18 days before the hearing, and opposing affidavits not less than 8 days before it, unless the rules or the court fix another time (Haw. R. Civ. P. 6(d)). The earlier outline named no Hawai'i pleading-standard decision."
  edge-pleading-motion-granted "Granted" -> dismissed { authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 12(b)" }
  edge-pleading-motion-amend "Leave to amend" -> amend { authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 15(a)" }
  edge-pleading-motion-denied "Denied: answer within 10 days of notice" -> discovery {
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 12(a)"
  }
}

state amend: "Amended pleading" by applicant cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 15(a)"
{
  note "A party may amend once as a matter of course before a responsive pleading is served; otherwise only by leave of court or by written consent of the adverse party, and leave is freely given when justice so requires. A motion or stipulation to amend carries the proposed amended pleading in Ramseyer format (Haw. R. Civ. P. 15(a))."
  edge-amend-tested "Amended pleading tested again" -> pleading-motion {
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 12(b)"
  }
}

terminal dismissed: "Dismissed on the pleadings" outcome [win, dismissal] cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 12(b)"
{
  note "Outcome from the defending side. Appeal of the resulting judgment runs under Haw. R. App. P. 4(a)."
}

decision default-entered: "Default" by court cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 55(a)"
{
  note "When a party against whom affirmative relief is sought has failed to plead or otherwise defend and that is shown by affidavit or otherwise, the clerk enters the party's default. The clerk enters default judgment for a sum certain against a defendant defaulted for failure to appear who is not an infant or incompetent person; in other cases the party applies to the court, and a party who has appeared is served with written notice of the application at least 3 days before the hearing on it (Haw. R. Civ. P. 55(a), (b)). For good cause shown the court may set aside an entry of default, and a default judgment in accordance with Rule 60(b) (Haw. R. Civ. P. 55(c)). The earlier outline named no set-aside decision."
  edge-default-entered-judgment "Default judgment entered" -> default-judgment {
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 55(b)"
  }
  edge-default-entered-set-aside "Default set aside for good cause" -> discovery {
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 55(c)"
  }
}

terminal default-judgment: "Default judgment" outcome [loss] cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 55(b)"
{
  note "Outcome from the defending side."
}

state discovery: "Disclosure, discovery and pretrial" by applicant cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 26(a)"
{
  note "A party makes its initial disclosures at or within 14 days after the parties' Rule 26(f) conference unless a different time is set by stipulation or court order, or a party objects during the conference (Haw. R. Civ. P. 26(a)(1)(C)). A party demands a jury by serving a written demand not later than 10 days after service of the last pleading directed to the issue and filing it as Rule 5(d) requires (Haw. R. Civ. P. 38(b))."
  edge-discovery-sj "Summary judgment motion" -> summary-judgment {
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 56"
  }
  edge-discovery-trial "No dispositive motion" -> trial { authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 38" }
  edge-discovery-settled "Stipulated dismissal" -> settled {
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 41(a)"
  }
}

decision summary-judgment: "Summary judgment decided" by court cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 56(c)"
{
  note "A claimant may move at any time after 20 days from commencement or after the adverse party moves; a defending party at any time; either motion is served and filed no less than 50 days before trial unless the court permits otherwise for good cause (Haw. R. Civ. P. 56(a), (b)). The motion is filed and served not less than 18 days before the hearing, the opposition not less than 8 days before it, and a reply not less than 3 days before it; judgment is rendered forthwith if there is no genuine issue as to any material fact and the movant is entitled to judgment as a matter of law (Haw. R. Civ. P. 56(c)). The earlier outline named no Hawai'i summary-judgment decision."
  edge-summary-judgment-granted "Granted" -> judgment-entered {
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 56(c)"
  }
  edge-summary-judgment-denied "Denied" -> trial { authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 56(c)" }
}

state trial: "Trial by jury or by the court" by court cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 38"
{
  note "Issues triable of right by a jury are so tried on a timely written demand (Haw. R. Civ. P. 38(b)). A renewed motion for judgment as a matter of law is filed no later than 10 days after entry of judgment, and may join a motion for a new trial under Rule 59 (Haw. R. Civ. P. 50(b))."
  edge-trial-judgment "Verdict or decision" -> post-trial { authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 58" }
  edge-trial-settled "Settled before verdict" -> settled { authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 41(a)" }
}

decision post-trial: "Post-trial motions" by applicant cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 59"
{
  note "A motion for a new trial, and a motion to alter or amend a judgment, are filed no later than 10 days after entry of the judgment; opposing affidavits follow within 10 days after service (Haw. R. Civ. P. 59(b), (c), (e)). A motion to amend findings is made not later than 10 days after entry of judgment (Haw. R. Civ. P. 52(b)). The court may not extend the time for action under Rules 50(b), 52(b), 59(b), (d) and (e) and 60(b) except as those rules state (Haw. R. Civ. P. 6(b)). A timely post-judgment motion of these kinds, or for attorney's fees or costs, extends the time to appeal as Haw. R. App. P. 4(a)(3) provides; the order of July 15, 2026 rewrites that subdivision effective January 1, 2027 (sources/hi-ica), so its periods are not stated here."
  edge-post-trial-resolved "Motions resolved or none filed" -> judgment-entered {
    event JudgmentEntered()
    authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 58"
  }
}

decision judgment-entered: "Final judgment entered" by office cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 58"
{
  note "Unless the court directs otherwise, the prevailing party prepares and submits a proposed judgment; filing in the clerk's office is entry, entry is not delayed for taxing costs, and every judgment is set forth on a separate document (Haw. R. Civ. P. 58). Costs may be taxed by the clerk on 48 hours' notice and reviewed on motion served within 5 days thereafter; a motion for attorneys' fees is filed and served no later than 14 days after entry of an appealable order or judgment unless a statute or order provides otherwise (Haw. R. Civ. P. 54(d)(1), (2)(B))."
  edge-judgment-entered-appeal "Notice of appeal within 30 days" -> appeal-taken {
    event NoticeOfAppealFiled()
    authority cite "Haw. R. App. P. 4(a)"
  }
  edge-judgment-entered-final "No appeal" -> final-no-appeal { authority cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 58" }
}

terminal appeal-taken: "Appeal taken: continue in the Hawai'i appellate package" outcome [appeal] cite "Haw. R. App. P. 4(a)"
{
  note "The notice of appeal is filed within 30 days after entry of the judgment or appealable order; a mailed notice is timely if postmarked within that time and received no later than 5 days after the postmark (Haw. R. App. P. 4(a)(1)). The court appealed from may extend the time for good cause on a motion filed within it, or for excusable neglect on a motion filed not later than 30 days after it expires, by no more than 30 days past the prescribed time (Haw. R. App. P. 4(a)(4)). A notice of cross-appeal is filed within 14 days after the notice of appeal is served on the cross-appellant, or within the time for the notice of appeal, whichever is later (Haw. R. App. P. 4.1(b)). Hand-off to lit/hi-ica (hi-appellate-civil)."
}

terminal final-no-appeal: "Final: no appeal" outcome [final] cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 58"

terminal settled: "Settled: dismissed by stipulation" outcome [settlement] cite "Haw. R. Civ. P. 41(a)"
{
  note "An action may be dismissed without order by a notice of dismissal before the return date under Rule 12(a) or service of an answer or summary judgment motion, or by a stipulation of dismissal signed by all parties who have appeared, in the form Rule 41.1 prescribes; it is without prejudice unless stated otherwise (Haw. R. Civ. P. 41(a)(1))."
}
